cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the archived reproducibility materials, please cite this software release and the accompanying article."
title: "Code and Reproducibility Materials for From Codebooks to Scalable Frame Detection with LLMs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Olier
    given-names: Juan Sebastian
    affiliation: "Department of Intelligent Systems, Tilburg University"
version: 1.0.2
date-released: 2026-10-02
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Python implementation and archived reproducibility materials for the study
  "From Codebooks to Scalable Frame Detection with LLMs: A Zero-Shot Approach
  via Binary Questions." The software implements binary indicator-question
  classification with open-source LLMs, full-frame-description prompting,
  sentence-similarity baselines, multi-model aggregation, and evaluation
  against the Gun Violence Frame Corpus (GVFC). Archived final predictions are
  included for reproducing the main binary-question results without rerunning
  LLM inference.
keywords:
  - framing analysis
  - large language models
  - zero-shot classification
  - computational communication
  - codebooks
  - reproducibility
  - natural language processing
